Just how bad is the penalty for body armor for a monk?

I've currently got a monk who stumbled upon GDSM.  I tried it
on, out of curiousity, and while every time I attack, I get the
message "Your armor is rather cumbersome...", it is always
followed by a "You hit ..." or "You kill ...".  And I've not
stumbled or had any of the other effects you usually get when
clumsy.  And that extra protection isn't to be sneezed at.

I've just cleaned out the castle.  For only about the third or
fourth time, and definitly the first as something other than
Samurai, Valyrie or Barbarian.  On the other hand, I'm only
XL17.  Wielding a +7 Snickersee---I know that Monks aren't
supposed to do that, but I since my god was nice enough to give
it to me...  And obviously, basic in long sword, and not going
to get any better.  (I didn't think monks could use weapons
effectively, but this one seems to be able to.)

I've got a fair number of blank scrolls, and two unused magic
markers, so if the GDSM isn't going to hurt my fighting ability
that much, I'll enchant it up... and end up playing monk exactly
like I play Valkyrie:-).  (It does piss me off a little that I
expended a wish for a cloak of magic protection.  I was sure
that was the only way to get it if you were a monk, and since
I'd lost my robe to a polymorph trap early on anyway...)

